   "ply": 18,
   "t": 915,
   "fen": "r3kb1r/pp1n1ppp/2p1pn2/q6b/8/2NP2PP/PPP1NPB1/R1BQ1RK1 w kq - 0 10",
   "line": [
    "e6"
   ],
   "spoken": "...Black plays e6.",
   "reanchor": true
  },
  {
   "ply": 19,
   "t": 918.5,
   "fen": "r3kb1r/pp1n1ppp/2p1pn2/q6b/8/P1NP2PP/1PP1NPB1/R1BQ1RK1 b kq - 0 10",
   "line": [
    "a3"
   ],
   "spoken": "Here we would have prepared with a3, readying b4.",
   "reanchor": true
  },
  {
   "ply": 20,
   "t": 921,
   "fen": "r3k2r/pp1nbppp/2p1pn2/q6b/8/P1NP2PP/1PP1NPB1/R1BQ1RK1 w kq - 1 11",
   "line": [
    "Be7"
   ],
   "spoken": "After the bishop to e7...",
   "reanchor": true
  },
  {
   "ply": 22,
   "t": 927,
   "fen": "r3k2r/pp1n1ppp/2p1pn2/q6b/1b6/P1NP2PP/2P1NPB1/R1BQ1RK1 w kq - 0 12",
   "line": [
    "b4",
    "Bxb4"
   ],
   "spoken": "...b4 immediately would run into the bishop capturing on b4 — a tactic to be aware of.",
   "reanchor": true
  },
  {
   "ply": 20,
   "t": 931.5,
   "fen": "r3k2r/pp1nbppp/2p1pn2/q6b/8/P1NP2PP/1PP1NPB1/R1BQ1RK1 w kq - 1 11",
   "line": [],
   "spoken": "So to play b4 there, we would first develop the bishop.",
   "reanchor": true
  },
  {
   "ply": 21,
   "t": 937,
   "fen": "r3k2r/pp1nbppp/2p1pn2/q6b/8/P1NPB1PP/1PP1NPB1/R2Q1RK1 b kq - 2 11",
   "line": [
    "Be3"
   ],
   "spoken": "The bishop to e3, for instance.",
   "reanchor": true
  },
  {
   "ply": 22,
   "t": 938.5,
   "fen": "r4rk1/pp1nbppp/2p1pn2/q6b/8/P1NPB1PP/1PP1NPB1/R2Q1RK1 w - - 3 12",
   "line": [
    "O-O"
   ],
   "spoken": "The line would run: castle...",
   "reanchor": true
  },
  {
   "ply": 23,
   "t": 942,
   "fen": "r4rk1/pp1nbppp/2p1pn2/q6b/1P6/P1NPB1PP/2P1NPB1/R2Q1RK1 b - - 0 12",
   "line": [
    "b4"
   ],
   "spoken": "...then b4.",
   "reanchor": true
  },
  {
   "ply": 24,
   "t": 944,
   "fen": "r4rk1/ppqnbppp/2p1pn2/7b/1P6/P1NPB1PP/2P1NPB1/R2Q1RK1 w - - 1 13",
   "line": [
    "Qc7"
   ],
   "spoken": "Black would retreat the queen to c7...",
   "reanchor": true
  },
  {
   "ply": 25,
   "t": 945,
   "fen": "r4rk1/ppqnbppp/2p1pn2/1P5b/8/P1NPB1PP/2P1NPB1/R2Q1RK1 b - - 0 13",
   "line": [
    "b5"
   ],
   "spoken": "...and b5 gets unpleasant for Black.",
   "reanchor": true
  },
  {
   "ply": 26,
   "t": 949,
   "fen": "r4rk1/ppqnbppp/4pn2/1Pp4b/8/P1NPB1PP/2P1NPB1/R2Q1RK1 w - - 0 14",
   "line": [
    "c5"
   ],
   "spoken": "If Black closes with c5, it opens the bishop's diagonal...",
   "reanchor": true
  },
  {
   "ply": 27,
   "t": 957,
   "fen": "r4rk1/ppqnbppp/4pn2/1Pp4b/P7/2NPB1PP/2P1NPB1/R2Q1RK1 b - - 0 14",
   "line": [
    "a4"
   ],
   "spoken": "...and we would storm exactly as in the game, pushing the a-pawn up to a6 — strong even without a king on that wing.",
   "reanchor": true
  },
  {
   "ply": 24,
   "t": 972.5,
   "fen": "r4rk1/ppqnbppp/2p1pn2/7b/1P6/P1NPB1PP/2P1NPB1/R2Q1RK1 w - - 1 13",
   "line": [],
   "spoken": "So White contends for a small but stable edge — simple and practical.",
   "reanchor": true
  },
  {
   "ply": 17,
   "t": 975.5,
   "fen": "r3kb1r/pp1npppp/2p2n2/q6b/8/2NP2PP/PPP1NPB1/R1BQ1RK1 b kq - 0 9",
   "line": [],
   "spoken": "Very simple.",
   "reanchor": true
  },
  {
   "ply": 16,
   "t": 977,
   "fen": "r3kb1r/pp1npppp/2p2n2/q6b/8/2N3PP/PPPPNPB1/R1BQ1RK1 w kq - 4 9",
   "line": [],
   "spoken": "I'd recommend doing your own research rather than just playing it blind.",
   "reanchor": true
  },
  {
   "ply": 15,
   "t": 982.5,
   "fen": "rn2kb1r/pp2pppp/2p2n2/q6b/8/2N3PP/PPPPNPB1/R1BQ1RK1 b kq - 3 8",
   "line": [],
   "spoken": "Use these speedrun games as a basis for a practical, low-theory line against the Scandinavian.",
   "reanchor": true
  },
  {
   "ply": 17,
   "t": 994.5,
   "fen": "r3kb1r/pp1npppp/2p2n2/q6b/8/2NP2PP/PPP1NPB1/R1BQ1RK1 b kq - 0 9",
   "line": [
    "Nbd7",
    "d3"
   ],
   "spoken": "After castling, the b4 push is essentially a no-brainer.",
   "reanchor": true
  },
  {
   "ply": 19,
   "t": 996.5,
   "fen": "2kr1b1r/pp1npppp/2p2n2/q6b/1P6/2NP2PP/P1P1NPB1/R1BQ1RK1 b - - 0 10",
   "line": [
    "O-O-O",
    "b4"
   ],
   "spoken": "The bigger idea: in the middlegame, sacrificing a pawn for a strong, lasting attack is rarely a real risk — the practical chances are worth it, whereas in an endgame a single pawn matters far more.",
   "reanchor": true
  },
  {
   "ply": 20,
   "t": 1473,
   "fen": "2kr1b1r/ppqnpppp/2p2n2/7b/1P6/2NP2PP/P1P1NPB1/R1BQ1RK1 w - - 1 11",
   "line": [
    "Qc7"
   ],
   "spoken": "Back to the setup — after the queen to c7.",
   "reanchor": true
  },
  {
   "ply": 19,
   "t": 1475,
   "fen": "2kr1b1r/pp1npppp/2p2n2/q6b/1P6/2NP2PP/P1P1NPB1/R1BQ1RK1 b - - 0 10",
   "line": [],
   "spoken": "Now an important subtlety, before Black takes on b4.",
   "reanchor": true
  },
  {
   "ply": 20,
   "t": 1476.5,
   "fen": "2kr1b1r/pp1npppp/2p2n2/7b/1q6/2NP2PP/P1P1NPB1/R1BQ1RK1 w - - 0 11",
   "line": [
    "Qxb4"
   ],
   "spoken": "If Black grabs with the queen on b4...",
   "reanchor": true
  },
  {
   "ply": 21,
   "t": 1481,
   "fen": "2kr1b1r/pp1npppp/2p2n2/7b/1q6/2NP2PP/P1P1NPB1/1RBQ1RK1 b - - 1 11",
   "line": [
    "Rb1"
   ],
   "spoken": "...the tempting rook to b1 is actually a mistake.",
   "reanchor": true
  },
  {
   "ply": 22,
   "t": 1490,
   "fen": "2kr1b1r/pp1npppp/2p2n2/8/1q6/2NP2PP/P1P1bPB1/1RBQ1RK1 w - - 0 12",
   "line": [
    "Bxe2"
   ],
   "spoken": "Because either the queen takes on c3 or the bishop takes on e2 — the knight is overloaded.",
   "reanchor": true
  },
  {
   "ply": 23,
   "t": 1497.5,
   "fen": "2kr1b1r/pp1npppp/2p2n2/8/1R6/2NP2PP/P1P1bPB1/2BQ1RK1 b - - 0 12",
   "line": [
    "Rxb4"
   ],
   "spoken": "So you would have to take the queen, and Black forces an endgame.",
   "reanchor": true
  },
  {
   "ply": 25,
   "t": 1500,
   "fen": "2kr1b1r/pp1npppp/2p2n2/8/1R6/2NP2PP/P1P2PB1/2BR2K1 b - - 0 13",
   "line": [
    "Bxd1",
    "Rxd1"
   ],
   "spoken": "White is still fine there, with attacking potential even in the endgame.",
   "reanchor": true
  },
  {
   "ply": 21,
   "t": 1507.5,
   "fen": "2kr1b1r/pp1npppp/2p2n2/7b/1q6/2NP2PP/P1P1NPB1/1RBQ1RK1 b - - 1 11",
   "line": [],
   "spoken": "But you'd rather not trade queens if you can help it.",
   "reanchor": true
  },
  {
   "ply": 20,
   "t": 1509,
   "fen": "2kr1b1r/pp1npppp/2p2n2/7b/1q6/2NP2PP/P1P1NPB1/R1BQ1RK1 w - - 0 11",
   "line": [],
   "spoken": "So this would be a good spot to play g4 instead.",
   "reanchor": true
  },
  {
   "ply": 21,
   "t": 1510,
   "fen": "2kr1b1r/pp1npppp/2p2n2/7b/1q4P1/2NP3P/P1P1NPB1/R1BQ1RK1 b - - 0 11",
   "line": [
    "g4"
   ],
   "spoken": "The g4 push would unpin the knight.",
   "reanchor": true
  },
  {
   "ply": 22,
   "t": 1513.5,
   "fen": "2kr1b1r/pp1npppp/2p2nb1/8/1q4P1/2NP3P/P1P1NPB1/R1BQ1RK1 w - - 1 12",
   "line": [
    "Bg6"
   ],
   "spoken": "After the bishop drops to g6...",
   "reanchor": true
  },
  {
   "ply": 23,
   "t": 1515,
   "fen": "2kr1b1r/pp1npppp/2p2nb1/8/1q4P1/2NP3P/P1P1NPB1/1RBQ1RK1 b - - 2 12",
   "line": [
    "Rb1"
   ],
   "spoken": "...you could calmly play the rook to b1 and keep attacking.",
   "reanchor": true
  },
  {
   "ply": 20,
   "t": 1520.5,
   "fen": "2kr1b1r/pp1npppp/2p2n2/7b/1q6/2NP2PP/P1P1NPB1/R1BQ1RK1 w - - 0 11",
   "line": [],
   "spoken": "Our opponent didn't go for that line — can't blame him.",
   "reanchor": true
  },
  {
   "ply": 19,
   "t": 1522,
   "fen": "2kr1b1r/pp1npppp/2p2n2/q6b/1P6/2NP2PP/P1P1NPB1/R1BQ1RK1 b - - 0 10",
   "line": [],
   "spoken": "The game continued with the queen to c7 and b5...",
   "reanchor": true
  },
  {
   "ply": 20,
   "t": 1523.5,
   "fen": "2kr1b1r/ppqnpppp/2p2n2/7b/1P6/2NP2PP/P1P1NPB1/R1BQ1RK1 w - - 1 11",
   "line": [
    "Qc7"
   ],
   "spoken": "...the queen to c7...",
   "reanchor": true
  },
  {
   "ply": 21,
   "t": 1524.5,
   "fen": "2kr1b1r/ppqnpppp/2p2n2/1P5b/8/2NP2PP/P1P1NPB1/R1BQ1RK1 b - - 0 11",
   "line": [
    "b5"
   ],
   "spoken": "...and b5.",
   "reanchor": true
  },
  {
   "ply": 23,
   "t": 1526,
   "fen": "2kr1b1r/ppqnpppp/5n2/1Pp4b/P7/2NP2PP/2P1NPB1/R1BQ1RK1 b - - 0 12",
   "line": [
    "c5",
    "a4"
   ],
   "spoken": "Then, textbook — we'd shove the pawn to provoke weaknesses, exactly as before.",
   "reanchor": true
  },
  {
   "ply": 25,
   "t": 1530,
   "fen": "2kr1b1r/p1qnpppp/1p3n2/PPp4b/8/2NP2PP/2P1NPB1/R1BQ1RK1 b - - 0 13",
   "line": [
    "b6",
    "a5"
   ],
   "spoken": "The pawn storm provokes the weaknesses we need.",
   "reanchor": true
  },
  {
   "ply": 23,
   "t": 1531.5,
   "fen": "2kr1b1r/ppqnpppp/5n2/1Pp4b/P7/2NP2PP/2P1NPB1/R1BQ1RK1 b - - 0 12",
   "line": [],
   "spoken": "How are pawns used in an attack? Two main ways — the first is to sacrifice them to open files and squares for your pieces.",
   "reanchor": true
  },
  {
   "ply": 26,
   "t": 1571,
   "fen": "2kr3r/ppqnbppp/4pn2/PPp4b/8/2NP2PP/2P1NPB1/R1BQ1RK1 w - - 1 14",
   "line": [
    "e6",
    "a5",
    "Be7"
   ],
   "spoken": "Let me show both uses.",
   "reanchor": true
  },
  {
   "ply": 27,
   "t": 1574,
   "fen": "2kr3r/ppqnbppp/1P2pn2/P1p4b/8/2NP2PP/2P1NPB1/R1BQ1RK1 b - - 0 14",
   "line": [
    "b6"
   ],
   "spoken": "The first is a move like b6 — the classic pawn-storm break, blasting things open.",
   "reanchor": true
  },
  {
   "ply": 28,
   "t": 1580.5,
   "fen": "2kr3r/1pqnbppp/1p2pn2/P1p4b/8/2NP2PP/2P1NPB1/R1BQ1RK1 w - - 0 15",
   "line": [
    "axb6"
   ],
   "spoken": "What does b6 accomplish?",
   "reanchor": true
  },
  {
   "ply": 31,
   "t": 1587.5,
   "fen": "1qkr3r/1p1nbppp/1P2pn2/1Np4b/8/3P2PP/2P1NPB1/R1BQ1RK1 b - - 2 16",
   "line": [
    "axb6",
    "Qb8",
    "Nb5"
   ],
   "spoken": "It hands the knight the b5 square and hands the rook the a-file — a pawn sacrificed for entry points.",
   "reanchor": true
  },
  {
   "ply": 26,
   "t": 1593,
   "fen": "2kr3r/ppqnbppp/4pn2/PPp4b/8/2NP2PP/2P1NPB1/R1BQ1RK1 w - - 1 14",
   "line": [],
   "spoken": "The second way is to create anchor points for your own pieces.",
   "reanchor": true
  },
  {
   "ply": 27,
   "t": 1600.5,
   "fen": "2kr3r/ppqnbppp/P3pn2/1Pp4b/8/2NP2PP/2P1NPB1/R1BQ1RK1 b - - 0 14",
   "line": [
    "a6"
   ],
   "spoken": "That would be a move like a6 — worse here, but it illustrates pawns as anchors.",
   "reanchor": true
  },
  {
   "ply": 28,
   "t": 1604,
   "fen": "2kr3r/p1qnbppp/Pp2pn2/1Pp4b/8/2NP2PP/2P1NPB1/R1BQ1RK1 w - - 0 15",
   "line": [
    "b6"
   ],
   "spoken": "You create entry points where a queen can sit, using the pawns to anchor your pieces.",
   "reanchor": true
  },
  {
   "ply": 26,
   "t": 1622.5,
   "fen": "2kr3r/ppqnbppp/4pn2/PPp4b/8/2NP2PP/2P1NPB1/R1BQ1RK1 w - - 1 14",
   "line": [],
   "spoken": "Pawns can even be attackers themselves — but a storm isn't always required; often pushing a single pawn to open one file is enough. Understand the goal, usually opening as many files as possible against the king, rather than shoving pawns blindly.",
   "reanchor": true
  },
  {
   "ply": 30,
   "t": 1898,
   "fen": "2kr1b1r/p1qn1ppp/1p2pn2/PPp4b/5B2/2NP2PP/2P1NPB1/R2Q1RK1 w - - 2 16",
   "line": [
    "Bd2",
    "b6",
    "Bf4",
    "Bf8"
   ],
   "spoken": "Skipping ahead — after a5 our play was all intuitive; the bishop to f4.",
   "reanchor": true
  },
  {
   "ply": 34,
   "t": 1903.5,
   "fen": "2kr3r/p1qn1ppp/1p1bpn2/PPp4b/5B2/2NP2PP/2P1NPB1/R2Q1RK1 w - - 6 18",
   "line": [
    "Bd6",
    "Be7",
    "Bf4",
    "Bd6"
   ],
   "spoken": "Then the take-order question after the bishop to d6.",
   "reanchor": true
  },
  {
   "ply": 37,
   "t": 1906,
   "fen": "2kr3r/p2n1ppp/1P1qpn2/1Pp4b/8/2NP2PP/2P1NPB1/R2Q1RK1 b - - 0 19",
   "line": [
    "Bxd6",
    "Qxd6",
    "axb6"
   ],
   "spoken": "We take on d6 first, then on b6 — not the other way round.",
   "reanchor": true
  },
  {
   "ply": 34,
   "t": 1908,
   "fen": "2kr3r/p1qn1ppp/1p1bpn2/PPp4b/5B2/2NP2PP/2P1NPB1/R2Q1RK1 w - - 6 18",
   "line": [],
   "spoken": "The order matters...",
   "reanchor": true
  },
  {
   "ply": 35,
   "t": 1909.5,
   "fen": "2kr3r/p1qn1ppp/1P1bpn2/1Pp4b/5B2/2NP2PP/2P1NPB1/R2Q1RK1 b - - 0 18",
   "line": [
    "axb6"
   ],
   "spoken": "...because if we take on b6 first, the knight would recapture on b6...",
   "reanchor": true
  },
  {
   "ply": 38,
   "t": 1911.5,
   "fen": "2k4r/p1q2ppp/1n1rpn2/1Pp4b/8/2NP2PP/2P1NPB1/R2Q1RK1 w - - 0 20",
   "line": [
    "Nxb6",
    "Bxd6",
    "Rxd6"
   ],
   "spoken": "...and Black holds by recapturing on d6 with the rook, keeping a7 defended. So we do it the other way.",
   "reanchor": true
  },
  {
   "ply": 37,
   "t": 1915.5,
   "fen": "2kr3r/p1q2ppp/1n1Bpn2/1Pp4b/8/2NP2PP/2P1NPB1/R2Q1RK1 b - - 0 19",
   "line": [],
   "spoken": "Take, take — and if the queen recaptures on b6...",
   "reanchor": true
  },
  {
   "ply": 40,
   "t": 1919,
   "fen": "2kr3r/p2q1ppp/Rn2pn2/1Pp4b/8/2NP2PP/2P1NPB1/3Q1RK1 w - - 2 21",
   "line": [
    "Qxd6",
    "Ra6",
    "Qd7"
   ],
   "spoken": "...we would have the rook to a6, incredibly strong, with the queen to a1 to follow.",
   "reanchor": true
  },
  {
   "ply": 41,
   "t": 1923,
   "fen": "2kr3r/p2q1ppp/1n2pn2/1Pp4b/8/2NP2PP/2P1NPB1/R2Q1RK1 b - - 3 21",
   "line": [
    "Ra1"
   ],
   "spoken": "The rook would lift along the a-file...",
   "reanchor": true
  },
  {
   "ply": 42,
   "t": 1925,
   "fen": "2kr3r/p4ppp/1n1qpn2/1Pp4b/8/2NP2PP/2P1NPB1/R2Q1RK1 w - - 4 22",
   "line": [
    "Qd6"
   ],
   "spoken": "...and the queen would support from behind.",
   "reanchor": true
  },
  {
   "ply": 30,
   "t": 1927.5,
   "fen": "2kr1b1r/p1qn1ppp/1p2pn2/PPp4b/5B2/2NP2PP/2P1NPB1/R2Q1RK1 w - - 2 16",
   "line": [],
   "spoken": "Why provoke e5? There's a positional point.",
   "reanchor": true
  },
  {
   "ply": 32,
   "t": 1946,
   "fen": "2kr1b1r/p1qn1ppp/1p3n2/PPp1p2b/8/2NPB1PP/2P1NPB1/R2Q1RK1 w - - 0 17",
   "line": [
    "Be3",
    "e5"
   ],
   "spoken": "Provoking e5 gains us the d5 square — attacking doesn't mean positional sense goes out the window.",
   "reanchor": true
  },
  {
   "ply": 36,
   "t": 1961,
   "fen": "2kr3r/p1qnbppp/1p3nb1/PPp1p1P1/8/2NPB2P/2P1NPB1/R2Q1RK1 w - - 1 19",
   "line": [
    "g4",
    "Be7",
    "g5",
    "Bg6"
   ],
   "spoken": "If Black plays the bishop to b7, we'd have g4 and g5 to build a monster on d5.",
   "reanchor": true
  },
  {
   "ply": 38,
   "t": 1963,
   "fen": "2kr2nr/p1qnbppp/1p4b1/PPpNp1P1/8/3PB2P/2P1NPB1/R2Q1RK1 w - - 3 20",
   "line": [
    "Nd5",
    "Ng8"
   ],
   "spoken": "A knight would land on d5 and the game is over — Black overwhelmed.",
   "reanchor": true
  },
  {
   "ply": 32,
   "t": 1972.5,
   "fen": "2kr1b1r/p1qn1ppp/1p3n2/PPp1p2b/8/2NPB1PP/2P1NPB1/R2Q1RK1 w - - 0 17",
   "line": [],
   "spoken": "When attacking, think about all parts of the board — the centre bears on the queenside.",
   "reanchor": true
  },
  {
   "ply": 36,
   "t": 1996.5,
   "fen": "2kr1b1r/p1qn1pp1/1p3nbp/PPp1p3/5PP1/2NPB2P/2P1N1B1/R2Q1RK1 w - - 1 19",
   "line": [
    "g4",
    "h6",
    "f4",
    "Bg6"
   ],
   "spoken": "Even if Black plays h6, the square is a long-term weakness — f4 could prise open another route, and a knight reaches d5.",
   "reanchor": true
  },
  {
   "ply": 34,
   "t": 2007.5,
